<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!-- THE WINDOW IS PITCH BLACK, IN EVERY SYSTEM MODE (owner, 2026-09-17:
         "Set a pure, pitch-black background across all screens").

         This one colour has to be repeated in XML because the WINDOW is painted
         before Compose draws its first frame and the framework cannot read a
         Compose ColorScheme. It has to equal EvColorScheme's `background` or the
         splash-to-Compose handover is a flash of colour rather than a change of
         content - so if one of them ever moves, move both.

         The value is still not invented: #000000 is PaletteTokens.Neutral0, read
         out of the pinned material3-android-1.4.0 jar's own bytecode, and it is
         what ComposeTheme.kt passes to darkColorScheme(background = ...).

         THERE IS NO values-night COPY ANY MORE. There was one, carrying the dark
         scheme's Neutral6 #141218, from the 2026-09-08 pass when the app followed
         the system. The app has one scheme again, so a night variant could only
         ever hold the same value twice - and two copies of one colour is exactly
         how a theme drifts. -->
    <color name="ev_background">#FF000000</color>
</resources>
